  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Build one material from a raw texture set, and use it in this corner.


    1. In Raw-Sets, pick a set. Set the normal map''s Texture Type to Normal map, and turn sRGB off on the ambient occlusion texture.

    2. Create a new material (URP Lit) in your own folder.

    3. Assign the Base Map, the Normal Map and the Occlusion Map.

    4. URP Lit uses smoothness, the opposite of roughness: set the Smoothness slider by eye, against the reference scenes.

    5. Set Tiling so the texture shows at its real size (concrete panels about 2.4 m, stone paving about 2 m).

    6. Apply it to the wall, the floor or the bench. Keep the material in your library.


    <b>Or:</b> start from your own photo of a surface in Milan.'
